016C                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
016C                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
016C                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
016C                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
016C                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
016C                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
